@startuml agent-lifecycle
' The Agent phase machine: every phase and the transition that moves between
' them, one trigger per edge. Triggers and their mechanics are the table on
' docs/src/controller/agent-lifecycle.md.
!include _style.puml

state Pending
state Provisioning
state Running
state Idle
state Hibernating
state Hibernated
state Resuming
state "any phase" as Any #F5F5F5
state Degraded
state Failed
state Terminating

[*] --> Pending
Pending --> Provisioning : Certificate created
Provisioning --> Running : Pod Ready
Running --> Idle : idleTimeout elapsed
Idle --> Running : activity observed
Idle --> Hibernating : hibernationDelay elapsed
Hibernating --> Hibernated : Pod gone
Hibernated --> Resuming : wake annotation
Resuming --> Provisioning : Pod created
Running --> Provisioning : spec drift,\nPod disruption
Idle --> Provisioning : spec drift,\nPod disruption

Any --> Degraded : class mismatch
Degraded --> Any : mismatch cleared
Any --> Failed : crash loop,\nimage pull
Any --> Terminating : deleted
Failed --> Provisioning : Pod recovers\nor is replaced
@enduml
